<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="OpenAI" Version="2.14.0"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\TokenGuard.Core\TokenGuard.Core.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>
    
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <Version>1.3.0</Version>
        <PackageId>TokenGuard.Extensions.OpenAI</PackageId>
        <Title>TokenGuard.Extensions.OpenAI</Title>
        <Authors>Svetlozar Stoykov</Authors>
        <Company>Svetlozar Stoykov</Company>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Svetlozar Stoykov</Copyright>
        <Description>OpenAI integration for TokenGuard on .NET 10. Converts prepared TokenGuard messages to OpenAI chat messages and lets TokenGuard use OpenAI to summarize older history when context gets tight. Targets net10.0 only.</Description>
        <PackageTags>tokenguard;openai;gpt;llm;ai;agents;context-management;token-budget;prompt-management;dotnet</PackageTags>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Requires TokenGuard.Core 1.3.0 or later, and OpenAI 2.14.0 or later. The summarizer implements Core's public ILlmSummarizer contract, so Core builds its transcript, request budget and response checks; a summarizer answer that is a refusal throws InvalidOperationException with the refusal text.

Behavior changes come from TokenGuard.Core 1.3.0, with no signature changes: a recorded tool result above a token limit is stored shortened; the compaction strategy receives its budget on the estimate scale, inverted from the provider correction; pretty-printed JSON is charged for its whitespace; a tool result is masked only when its placeholder is smaller; the summarizer request is built to a token budget and its output cap is twice the target; summarizer diagnostics name the summarizer type and normalize finish reasons. Prepared views can differ from those of 1.2.0 for the same history.

Known limits: one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas until the first provider report; with the tool result limit turned off, one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.

Full details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
    </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
